{"after_gate_rev": null, "author_time": 1448386167, "commit": "5f98f570c08a11e607cccfd9c1b787c69a6a67b7", "id": "click-5f98f570c08a", "issue": {"body": "Hi,\n\nconsider the following program\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python\nimport click\n@click.command()\n@click.argument('one',nargs = 2, default = (1,2))\ndef cmd(one):\n  print \"  => one: {}\".format(one)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n  cmd()\n```\n\nif you run it without parameters click maps  `(None,None)` to  `one`, while I would have expected `one` to have the value `(1,2)`\n\nis this intentional?\n\nThanks,\nLukas\n", "number": 463, "title": "defaults for arguments with nargs>1 not picked up"}, "issue_fetch": "ok", "parent": "0a2919f34fcbc635d8530b4c5b60bf119b2bcedb", "pr": null, "probe": {}, "prompt_subject": "Resolve the GitHub issue below.", "repo": "click", "shape": "symptom", "stats": {"code_files": 4, "code_lines": 164, "test_files": 1}, "subject": "Implemented defaults for args with nargs > 1.", "truth": {"code": [{"hunks": [[44, 1], [81, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "click/__init__.py", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[168, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "click/exceptions.py", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[19, 2], [23, 1], [25, 2], [118, 0], [216, 2], [278, 1], [286, 1], [318, 1]], "old_path": null, "path": "click/parser.py", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[3, 1], [26, 64]], "old_path": null, "path": "click/utils.py", "status": "M"}], "other": ["CHANGES"], "tests": ["tests/test_arguments.py"]}}
