{"after_gate_rev": null, "author_time": 1401909645, "commit": "264fa24d40725f3278d9a783c84cf8bf2d333300", "id": "click-264fa24d4072", "issue": {"body": "When a required choice is not present, the message is not very helpful for a new user:\n\n```\npython.exe test3.py\nUsage: test3.py [OPTIONS] [ARG1]...\n\nError: Missing option \"-o1\" / \"--option1\".\n```\n\nSo he would have to pass something for it:\n\n```\npython.exe test3.py -o1 abc\nUsage: test3.py [OPTIONS] [ARG1]...\n\nError: Invalid value for \"-o1\" / \"--option1\": invalid choice: abc. (choose from QA, UAT, PROD)\n```\n\nIs it possible to show the full help (that includes the valid options for the required choice) below the existing usage/error message?\n", "number": 120, "title": "add option for displaying full help when missing required args"}, "issue_fetch": "ok", "parent": "a6136b4079f52f4384fc8321672cf95b780527f8", "pr": null, "probe": {}, "prompt_subject": "Resolve the GitHub issue below.", "repo": "click", "shape": "symptom", "stats": {"code_files": 2, "code_lines": 16, "test_files": 1}, "subject": "Implemented extra info for missing choice parameters.  This fixes #120", "truth": {"code": [{"hunks": [[903, 1], [907, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "click/core.py", "status": "M"}, {"hunks": [[41, 0], [114, 0]], "old_path": null, "path": "click/types.py", "status": "M"}], "other": ["CHANGES"], "tests": ["tests/test_options.py"]}}
